<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/CoastalLagoons/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A04::CoastalLagoons";
        dc:date                "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:A04::CoastalLagoons";
        pav:authoredOn         "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/CoastalLagoons/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A01/current/Habitat_Alteration/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A01/current/Natural_Processes/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/NaturalCoastalFeatures/>;
        skos:definition        "Areas of relatively shallow, quiet water with access to the sea but separated from it by sandbars, barrier islands, or coral reefs. Coastal lagoons have low to moderate tides and constitute about 13% of the world's coastline. Their water is colder than the sea in winter and warmer in summer. In warm regions, evaporation may more than balance any freshwater input and may result in hypersaline water and even the buildup of thick salt deposits. Coral-reef lagoons occur on marginal reefs such as the Great Barrier Reef, but the most spectacular examples, some more than 30 mi (50 km) across, are associated with Pacific atolls."@en , "Las áreas relativamente poco profundas, con agua tranquila y acceso al mar, pero separado de él por bancos de arena, barreras de islas, o arrecifes de coral. Las lagunas costeras tienen unas mareas bajas o moderadas, y constituyen cerca del 13% de línea costera del mundo. Su agua es más fría que la marina en invierno y más cálida en verano. En las regiones más cálidas, el balance de la evaporación puede ser equilibrada por la introducción de agua fresca, así como puede resultar agua hipersalina, llegando a suponer depósitos de sal. Las lagunas de arrecife de coral, ocurren en los márgenes de los arrecifes como puede ser las Gran Barrera de Arrecife de Coral (Australia), pero los ejemplos mas espectaculares, algo mas de 50 km, están asociados a los atolones del Pacifico."@es;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/MIDA/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:A04::CoastalLagoons";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Coastal Lagoons"@en , "Lagunas costeras"@es .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/LandCover/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A04::LandCover";
        dc:date                "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:A04::LandCover";
        pav:authoredOn         "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/LandCover/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Landcover";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/LandUse/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/Landscape/>;
        skos:definition        "La cubierta biofísica observable de la superficie terrestre. Describe superficie vegetal y la antropica, omitiendo las rocas y la superficie acuática."@es , "The observed biophysical cover of the earth's surface. It describes vegetative and and man-made features, and omits bare rock and water. In practice, these elements are often included under this term."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/MIDA/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/>;
        skos:narrower          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/Semi-NaturalHabitat/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/LandCoverChange/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/BuiltUpAreas/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:A04::LandCover";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Cobertura terrestre"@es , "Land Cover"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/Semi-NaturalHabitat/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A04::Semi-NaturalHabitat";
        dc:date                "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:A04::Semi-NaturalHabitat";
        pav:authoredOn         "2012-06-27 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/Semi-NaturalHabitat/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/LandCover/>;
        skos:definition        "Los hábitats seminaturales son considerados a nivel mundial como cualquier hábitat donde los cambios inducidos por humanos se puede detectar, pero que aún parece un hábitat natural en términos de diversidad de especies y la complejidad de la interrelación especies."@es , "Semi-natural habitats are globally considered as any habitat where human induced changes can be detected or that is human managed but which still seems a natural habitat in terms of species diversity and species interrelation complexity."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/MIDA/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:A04::Semi-NaturalHabitat";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Hábitats seminaturales"@es , "Semi-Natural Habitat"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/ShippingPorts/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:A04::ShippingPorts";
